<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gustavia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gustavia is the capital and main harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-barthelemy">Saint Barthélemy</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. Known under French rule as Le Carénage, it was renamed after King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-iii">Gustav III</a> when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ceded the island to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1784, and the Swedes declared it a free port in 1785. Saint Barthélemy returned to France in 1878.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gustavia.jpg" alt="Gustavia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Originally uploaded at en.wikipedia by Evaneggers as en:Image:Stb.jpg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustavia_Harbor,_Saint-Barth%C3%A9lemy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
